 "intro_html": "Japanese rice balls. The rice is <b>plain</b> short-grain rice, seasoned only by the salt on your hands — not <a href=\"sushi-rice.html\">sushi rice</a>, which is vinegared and too soft and sharp for this. Shape them <b>by hand</b> (left hand underneath, right hand the roof) or <b>with a mold</b>; fill them with the classics or something louder. The juicier ones have their own pages: <a href=\"yaki-onigiri.html\">yaki onigiri</a> (a crisp soy-glazed crust), <a href=\"nikumaki-onigiri.html\">nikumaki onigiri</a> (wrapped in glazed pork belly), <a href=\"shrimp-karaage-onigiri.html\">shrimp karaage onigiri</a> (craggy fried shrimp + spicy mayo), <a href=\"onigirazu.html\">onigirazu</a> (the rice sandwich), <a href=\"spam-musubi.html\">spam musubi</a>, <a href=\"baby-octopus-onigiri.html\">baby octopus onigiri</a> (octopus rice, all inside) and <a href=\"salmon-onigiri.html\">salmon onigiri</a> (salmon through the rice, ikura in the center).",
