   "time": "~5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~5 min</span>",
   "title": "Wet and salt your hands",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "a little for each onigiri",
     "name_html": "Kosher salt (for your hands)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Scoop ~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"50\" data-s=\"0\">50 g</span> warm rice onto your LEFT palm — the left hand always stays underneath.</li><li>Press a small well in the middle and put in <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-b=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">1–2 tsp</span> of one filling.</li><li>Cover with another ~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"50\" data-s=\"0\">50 g</span> of rice and press it gently round the filling into a ball.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-5",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Rice, filling, close",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "About 50 g of warm rice on your left palm; press a small well into the middle.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/5-how1.webp?v=a2447717ab"
     },
     {
      "caption": "1–2 tsp of filling in the well, then cover with more rice.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/5-how2.webp?v=c3e8771711"
     }
    ],
