   "title": "Press the triangle",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Line a small bowl with plastic wrap and sprinkle in a little salt.</li><li>Rice in, a well, the filling, more rice on top, a little more salt.</li><li>Gather and twist the wrap shut, then press the same triangle through it. Good for lunchboxes — nobody’s hands touch the rice.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-7",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Or: through plastic wrap",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Rice and filling on plastic wrap in a bowl; gather and twist it shut, then press the triangle.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/7-how1.webp?v=7bfd4fb88d"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/onigiri/7.webp?v=44a93107e2",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 7,
   "part": "Shape by hand",
   "part_id": "part-shape-by-hand",
   "time": "~1 min each",
   "time_html": "<span>~1 min each</span>",
   "title": "Or: through plastic wrap",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Dip the mold and its lid in water, shake off the excess, and sprinkle salt inside.</li><li>Fill it halfway with warm rice, pushing it into the corners.</li><li>A spoonful of filling in the middle, then rice to the brim and a little salt on top.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-8",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Fill the mold",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Fill the wet mold halfway, pushing the rice into the corners.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/8-how1.webp?v=c42ae1f5d0"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Filling in the middle, then rice to the brim.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/8-how2.webp?v=ae64c7a07c"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/onigiri/8.webp?v=f3441ab996",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 8,
   "part": "Shape with a mold",
   "part_id": "part-shape-with-a-mold",
   "time": "~1 min each",
   "time_html": "<span>~1 min each</span>",
   "title": "Fill the mold",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Lid on and push down firmly — you should feel a slight resistance. No resistance? Add a little rice.</li><li>Lid off, flip the mold over the tray and push the button to pop the onigiri out.</li><li>Wet your fingers before touching it. A mold makes smaller, denser onigiri (~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"75\" data-s=\"0\">75 g</span> each, 13 from the pot); a lighter push keeps them fluffier.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-9",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Press and push out",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Lid on and press down firmly — stop when you feel resistance.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/9-how1.webp?v=3811fd7ac5"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Flip it over and push the button to pop the onigiri out.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/9-how2.webp?v=d686c3937e"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/onigiri/9.webp?v=d2b1350720",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 9,
   "part": "Shape with a mold",
   "part_id": "part-shape-with-a-mold",
   "time": "~30 s each",
   "time_html": "<span>~30 s each</span>",
   "title": "Press and push out",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Wrap a third of a nori sheet round the bottom of each onigiri — <b>right before eating</b> for crisp nori, or now for soft nori that sticks.</li><li>Or skip the nori: coat the three faces in <a href=\"furikake.html\">furikake</a> with wet fingers.</li><li>A little of the filling on the tip tells you what’s inside. Eat warm or at room temperature, within about 6 hours.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-10",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Nori, furikake, a dab on top",
